cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "sa-sme-data: what South Africa's public data says about small business and entrepreneurship"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible evidence base on South African small business: the source inventory,
  the counts and size distribution of informal and formal businesses, who employs
  people and why, fourteen years of informal-sector trend, and what the state spends.
  Derived from Statistics South Africa unit records, SARS/National Treasury tax
  statistics, and National Treasury budget and procurement data.
